# QA evidence screenshots — regenerable Playwright captures.
# NOT unreferenced: the August 2026 responsive audit cited sixteen paths inside
# this directory as its evidence. That audit was deleted on 2026-09-05 and its
# surviving facts are in docs/qa/defect-register-2026-08.md, which carries the
# method to regenerate these. They are deliberately not tracked
# (11 MB of PNGs that go stale the moment the stylesheet they document
# changes), so those citations record what was captured and at which width
# rather than linking a file you can open. Regenerate with the Method
# section of that audit.
#
# docs/qa/screenshots-mobile/ WAS tracked and was deleted on 2026-09-14: 4.3 MB
# of evidence for the sixteen defects of the 2026-08-26 mobile audit (#268),
# every one of them since fixed, showing a UI that no longer exists. The written
# findings survive in defect-register-2026-08.md, which is the part that was
# load-bearing. Both directories are now the same policy: the register records
# what was captured and at which width, and the capture itself is regenerable.
docs/qa/screenshots/
docs/qa/screenshots-mobile/

# Throwaway audit/probe scripts run from the repo root (module resolution
# needs them here). Never committed.
__*.mjs
__*.py

# Third-party skills installed by `npx skills add` (2026-09-03:
# Leonxlnx/taste-skill, 13 skills). This is a package manager's install
# directory — treat it like node_modules and reinstall rather than commit.
#
# Two concrete reasons, not a preference:
#   1. `npx skills add` symlinks .claude/skills/<name> -> .agents/skills/<name>
#      with an ABSOLUTE target (a path on one machine). Committed, those
#      links resolve to nothing on any other machine and in CI.
#   2. Git on Windows handles symlinks poorly — without core.symlinks=true they
#      land as plain text files containing a path, which is worse than absent
#      because it looks like content.
#
# How they are used, and where the codebase overrides them, is documented in
# docs/reference/doc-authority-map.md. Reinstall with:
#   npx skills add Leonxlnx/taste-skill
.agents/
.claude/skills/brandkit
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend-v1
.claude/skills/full-output-enforcement
.claude/skills/gpt-taste
.claude/skills/high-end-visual-design
.claude/skills/image-to-code
.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile
.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-web
.claude/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui
.claude/skills/minimalist-ui
.claude/skills/redesign-existing-projects
.claude/skills/stitch-design-taste
# pbakaus/impeccable, added 2026-09-04 by the same package manager.
.claude/skills/impeccable
# ...and the lockfile that package manager writes alongside them.
skills-lock.json
tests/flakeprobe-a0e1/artifacts/

# local screenshot harness (agent scratch)
shoot-tmp.mjs
mi-tmp.mjs

# scripts/firebase-deferral-trial.mjs — temporary copies of the two gated
# contexts with docs/design/firebase-deferral-gated.patch applied, plus the
# wrapper config that aliases them in. All three are deleted when it finishes;
# ignored so a crashed run cannot leave a second auth implementation in the
# tree looking like reviewed code.
src/**/*.trial.jsx
vite.config.trial.mjs
.firebase-deferral-trial.patch

# Scratch directories the gated-patch appliers use. Both copy the founder-gated
# files somewhere writable, apply a diff there, and delete the directory in a
# `finally` — these lines exist so a crashed run cannot leave a half-patched
# copy of firestore.rules sitting in `git status` looking like reviewed code.
.tmp-rules-patch-*/
.tmp-gated-patch-*/
.tmp-gated-diff-*/

# Impeccable live-mode session state and journal. Durable for the tool,
# not project source, and it holds absolute machine paths.
.impeccable/

# Screenshots and image archives — LOCAL ONLY.
#
# Measured 2026-09-15: screenshots/ was 8.7 MB across 27 tracked files, and
# eleven of the fifteen largest tracked files in the whole repository were the
# June portfolio archive. Nothing under src/, scripts/, api/, tests/ or public/
# reads any of them — the only references are three prose mentions in docs/,
# which describe what the shots showed rather than embedding them.
#
# They are kept on disk and out of git: a design archive is worth having and is
# not worth carrying in every clone, every CI checkout and every deploy.
screenshots/
*.psd
*.sketch
*.fig

# THE INTERNAL BOARDS AND THEIR ARCHIVE — LOCAL ONLY. On disk, out of git.
#
# This repository went PUBLIC on 2026-09-16, to use free GitHub Actions minutes.
# That made the engineering backlog world-readable, and the backlog is not a
# feature list: its `note` fields are candid internal prose written for us —
# security findings that are still open, instructions addressed to the owner,
# plans that were rejected and the reason, and the founder's own decisions in
# his own words.
#
# The founder chose, 2026-09-16, to KEEP THE REPOSITORY PUBLIC and take the
# notes out of it, rather than take the repository private. He accepted the cost
# in the same breath: the admin Pipeline and Board tabs have no data in
# production, because these three files are what they read.
#
#   src/data/pipeline.js                     the live backlog, 39 rows
#   src/data/moduleBoard.js                  per-module health and owner actions
#   docs/backlog/archive-done-2026-09-16.js  the 172 archived finished rows
#
# THEY ARE STILL ON DISK AND MUST STAY THERE. `git rm --cached` untracked them
# byte-identical; the founder's local checkout still serves both boards from
# them, and several tests still run in full wherever they are present. Deleting
# them is not what these lines mean.
#
# WHAT HAPPENS WITHOUT THEM: serveBacklog() in api/ai.js catches
# ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for exactly these two specifiers and answers 501 with
# `localOnly: true`, and both Admin tabs render that as a plain sentence saying
# the boards are local-only — never as an empty board, which would read as "no
# work left". Tests that need them SKIP WITH A STATED REASON rather than passing
# quietly on nothing.
#
# THIS DOES NOT REMOVE THEM FROM GIT HISTORY. Every commit up to this one still
# carries them, and they stay readable to anyone who clones. Rewriting history
# is a separate decision and has not been taken.
src/data/pipeline.js
src/data/moduleBoard.js
docs/backlog/archive-done-2026-09-16.js

# THE OWNER'S OWN DOCUMENTS — LOCAL ONLY. On disk, out of git.
#
# The same repository, the same day, the second half of the same decision. The
# founder, 2026-09-16, verbatim: "review whats in the public repo as this is
# now public, anything sensative should be stored locally."
#
# ONE OF THESE FOUR IS A SECURITY CALL AND THREE ARE NOT, and recording them as
# though they were the same thing is how the reason for a rule gets forgotten.
# So they are recorded separately.
#
#   docs/OWNER-ACTIONS.md
#
#     THE ONE THAT MATTERS. It is not a plan. It is the founder's own console
#     and credential worklist, row by row, with the exact step beside each.
#     In a private repository that is a to-do list. In a public one it is a
#     worklist, and nothing guarantees the founder is the first to read it.
#     What its rows say is not repeated here, and that is the point of this
#     block: an earlier version of this comment itemised them, which was the
#     disclosure one level up, and it is gone.
#
#   docs/PROPOSALS.md
#   docs/MARKETING.md
#   docs/qa/defect-register-2026-08.md
#
#     COMMERCIAL CAUTION, which is a different and a smaller reason, and saying
#     so is the point of listing them apart. Unreleased product proposals still
#     waiting on a founder verdict; how we intend to take this to market and
#     which half of each campaign is his to write; and the register of defects
#     we know about and have not fixed. Nothing in them is exploitable. They are
#     competitive and reputational — he would rather a competitor, or a
#     first-time visitor, did not meet the roadmap and the bug list first.
#
# THEY ARE STILL ON DISK AND MUST STAY THERE. `git rm --cached` untracked them
# byte-identical; the founder's own checkout still has all four and every test
# below runs in full there. Deleting them is not what these lines mean.
#
# WHAT HAPPENS WITHOUT THEM: three unit tests assert against the TEXT of
# OWNER-ACTIONS.md — that it names the `provider` value that means PASS, that it
# still names the one command which applies the gated patches, and that it
# quotes the derived Stripe product description rather than a paraphrase. Each
# SKIPS WITH A STATED REASON when the file is absent and runs in full when it is
# present; none of them passes quietly on nothing.
# tests/unit/doc-file-references.test.js resolves the paths documents name
# against the GIT INDEX rather than the working tree, and scans the same set of
# documents a clone has, so it reaches the same verdict on the founder's machine
# as on a public runner.
#
# THE DOCUMENTS THAT POINT AT THEM STILL SAY WHAT THEY ARE. Every reference was
# annotated, not deleted: a reader of the public repository is still told that
# an owner-actions register exists, what it holds and why it is not here.
# Removing the link as well would leave the next agent re-deriving a document
# that already exists.
#
# THIS DOES NOT REMOVE THEM FROM GIT HISTORY. Every commit up to this one still
# carries all four and they stay readable to anyone who clones. Rewriting
# history is a separate operation, already approved and scheduled, and is not
# what this commit does.
docs/OWNER-ACTIONS.md
docs/PROPOSALS.md
docs/MARKETING.md
docs/qa/defect-register-2026-08.md

# THE WORKING NOTES, THE AGENT TOOLING AND THE RELEASE RECORD — LOCAL ONLY.
# On disk, out of git.
#
# The same repository, the same day, the third and widest cut. The founder,
# 2026-09-16, verbatim: "can we remove claude files from the repo? and other
# files that expose the full innerworkings of our business. yes the app can be
# open source but the know how and usage of it in the UIL4B web format is
# owned by us" — and, of the Markdown: "these are in the app for our usage but
# dont need to be in the deployed files, review every deployed file and make
# sure the only ones that are publicly visable is whatever needs to be for the
# actual running of the app."
#
# That is the line, and it is a simple one: the SOURCE is public; how the
# business is run, how he works, and the method behind the design are not.
# Everything below fails the "needed to run the app" test — the build, the
# lint and the unit suite were run against a fresh clone without any of it.
#
#   CLAUDE.md                     how he works, in his words; the agent contract
#   PRODUCT.md                    the Impeccable product record
#   DESIGN.md                     the generated token mirror Impeccable reads,
#                                 and the design reasoning around it
#   CHANGELOG.md                  the release record — his decision, over
#                                 keeping it public: it carries his verbatim
#                                 quotes, the pricing calls and the commercial
#                                 reasoning behind every release
#   .mcp.json                     which MCP servers the agents run
#   .claude/                      the five agent roles and the seven project
#                                 skills — the method itself. The whole
#                                 directory, which also covers the third-party
#                                 skill lines above and the worktrees.
#   docs/reference/               the fifteen engineering and process references
#   docs/design/*.md              the homepage spec, the hero review, the
#                                 founder's motion reference, the deferral design
#   docs/research/                the homepage pattern research
#   docs/build-plan/              the tool tree
#   brand/email/                  the mailbox kit — his signature, the unsent
#                                 templates, and a README that named what the
#                                 mail path still lacked
#   scripts/design-md.mjs         the DESIGN.md generator; its prose IS the file
#   tests/unit/claude-md-external-assets.test.js
#   tests/unit/design-md-mirrors-css.test.js
#                                 two tests whose whole subject is a file above;
#                                 neither can run where the file is not
#
# WHAT STAYS, AND WHY. docs/design/*.patch stay tracked: scripts/gated-patches.mjs,
# tests/rules/ and three unit tests read them, so without them the rules suite
# does not run. They are code, not notes. tests/ stays whole: the suite is the
# product's contract and is what proves the app works. README.md stays because
# a public repository needs one. package.json keeps `design:md`; the generator
# it names is on the founder's machine.
#
# THEY ARE STILL ON DISK AND MUST STAY THERE. `git rm --cached` untracked every
# one of them byte-identical (SHA-256 checked before and after), and a second
# copy of each sits outside the repository. Deleting them is not what these
# lines mean.
#
# WHAT HAPPENS WITHOUT THEM: tests/unit/gate-doc.test.js reads
# docs/reference/build-and-verify.md and tests/unit/moderation-role.test.js
# reads docs/reference/human-validation-zones.md — each SKIPS WITH A STATED
# REASON where the document is absent and runs in full where it is present,
# exactly as the three OWNER-ACTIONS tests above do. The halves of those tests
# that read code rather than the document still run everywhere.
# tests/unit/doc-file-references.test.js scans the documents a clone has, which
# is now README.md, and its controls were re-baselined to that set — not
# loosened: every name below is held in LOCAL_ONLY_DOCS and proved ignored.
#
# SOURCE COMMENTS STILL CITE THESE FILES BY PATH — `Docs: design-language-v2.md`
# in global.css, `human-validation-zones.md` beside the founder-gated files, and
# so on, in some sixty files. Those are citations of documents on the founder's
# machine, left as they are: rewriting a hundred comments to say "local-only"
# says nothing this block does not already say, and a reader who does not have
# the file should ask him rather than reconstruct it.
#
# THIS DOES NOT REMOVE THEM FROM GIT HISTORY. Every commit up to this one still
# carries all of them. The history rewrite is a separate operation, approved,
# and scheduled to run after this lands; the full path list it needs is in the
# pull request that made this change.
CLAUDE.md
PRODUCT.md
DESIGN.md
CHANGELOG.md
.mcp.json
.claude/
docs/reference/
docs/design/*.md
docs/research/
docs/build-plan/
brand/email/
scripts/design-md.mjs
tests/unit/claude-md-external-assets.test.js
tests/unit/design-md-mirrors-css.test.js
